title: 'Migrate `pallet-election-provider-multi-phase` from the deprecated `ValidateUnsigned` trait to `#[pallet::authorize]`'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-election-provider-multi-phase` no longer uses the deprecated `ValidateUnsigned` trait and
    the `#[pallet::validate_unsigned]` attribute. The validation of `submit_unsigned` moved to a
    `#[pallet::authorize]` callback.

    The validation semantics do not change. The callback accepts only `TransactionSource::Local` and
    `TransactionSource::InBlock`, it runs the same pre-dispatch checks, and it builds the same
    transaction validity as before.

    Two changes affect a runtime that includes this pallet. The `Config` supertrait changed from
    `CreateBare<Call<Self>>` to `CreateAuthorizedTransaction<Call<Self>>`, and the runtime must put
    `frame_system::AuthorizeCall` in its transaction extension pipeline. `submit_unsigned` now needs
    an authorized origin.

crates:
- name: pallet-election-provider-multi-phase
  bump: major
- name: pallet-staking-async-rc-runtime
  bump: major
